Z||000000||Adam Draper||04-09-2001||09:13 PM||||   Okay I was on my way to hell (school) this morning when something like my tire lefted a part that would hit my floor panel. But even at idle it would do that pop pop pop. I could feel every pop in the floor panel, So I x out the tire not completely.<BR>I think it might be the pipes that ran to the radiator getting very hot and exploding.<BR>But I don't know if that is possible cuase my radiator is in poor shape I took it to work and it almost overheated on me on way home from work. I just paid some guy to fix my radiator I paid 58$ althought it looks new . can any you help me with this problem.<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||Old Lar||04-09-2001||09:56 PM||||I'm not sure what you are asking. I x out the tire???<P>The coolant tubes would not get hot and explode, the brackets that attaches them to he body may be loose and the loose pipe is hitting the floor.<P>If the radiator was repaced, the coolant system may not have been filled properly, and need to be burped.  Do a search of Fiero radiators as to proper filling procedure.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Adam Draper||04-10-2001||12:00 AM||||   No the radiator was fixed but the tubs were very weak the guy told me that the radiator will only last for 2 months. It didn't even last a day. my radiator leaks real bad and steams. I got under the car and my pipes were also sizzling in the pips you can hear the water boiling. That why I think that the pips are the cause of the sound. <BR>x out means I check off the tire, tire not the problem, delet tire theory.||||reg||10
Z||000003||sqoach||04-10-2001||12:09 AM||||This is just a guess, but I think that "popping" that you're hearing the the converter. It's probably clogged up and that would explain your overheating. I saw this on a friends van once. We heard a popping noise and I looked under it and saw the converter popping in and out every time he hit the gas!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>I would look under there to see if you see anything popping or something.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily overheating)||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||04-10-2001||01:27 AM||||If the car is on the hot side when you hear those pops the chances are good it is the coolant boiling in the pipes. If that is the case then every morning (engine cool) fill the puppy up and keep the overflow tank full as well. If you have AC and it doesnt work switch it on anyway cause it kicks on the fan full time.<P>||||reg||1
